CHAPTER.VERS:
Let them therefore, he says, who are of power among you

          {+}
         go down with me, and if there is anything amiss in the man, let them accuse him.

And Festus says, King Agrippa, and all men who are here present with us, you

          {+}
         see this man, about whom all the multitude of the Jews made suit to me, both at Jerusalem and here, crying that he ought not to live any longer.

Of whom I have no certain thing to write to my lord. Therefore I have brought him forth before you

          {+}
        , and especially before you, King Agrippa, that, after having the examination, I may have somewhat to write.
